From: Brad House <bhouse@nexthop.ai>
Subject: network: backport ManageForeignNextHops=

From v256. With ManageForeignNextHops=no, networkd ignores nexthops it
did not configure, so it no longer deletes a routing daemon's nexthop
groups when configuring a link. As in v256, [NextHop] then needs Id=.

Forwarded: https://github.com/systemd/systemd-stable/pull/499
Bug-Ubuntu: https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/systemd/+bug/2174541
Last-Update: 2026-11-15
---
diff --git a/man/networkd.conf.xml b/man/networkd.conf.xml
index 018bde0..65b1fe8 100644
--- a/man/networkd.conf.xml
+++ b/man/networkd.conf.xml
@@ -90,6 +90,17 @@
         <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v246"/></listitem>
       </varlistentry>
 
+      <varlistentry>
+        <term><varname>ManageForeignNextHops=</varname></term>
+        <listitem><para>A boolean. When true, <command>systemd-networkd</command> will remove nexthops
+        that are not configured in .network files (except for nexthops with protocol
+        <literal>kernel</literal>). When false, it will not remove any foreign nexthops, keeping them even
+        if they are not configured in a .network file. When false, [NextHop] sections in .network files
+        must have <varname>Id=</varname> set. Defaults to yes.</para>
+
+        <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v256"/></listitem>
+      </varlistentry>
+
       <varlistentry>
         <term><varname>RouteTable=</varname></term>
         <listitem><para>Defines the route table name. Takes a whitespace-separated list of the pairs of
